:: Wolf Cave Bailey Wolfsuit

A figure stumbles into the cave mouth, doubled over and panting. The wolves' ears prick up.
<br><br>

<<npc Bailey>><<person1>><span class="bailey-red">It's Bailey.</span> <<He>>'s wearing what appears to be a wolf costume. The suit is visibly too small. One ear is bent. The tail drags on the ground.
<br><br>

"It's time to pay up." <<He>> pauses, <<his>> eyes darting to the wolves around you, who have somehow yet to notice the intruder. "I mean. Woof."
<br><br>

The Black Wolf raises its head. It stares at Bailey for a long, uncomfortable moment.
<br><br>

Bailey stares back.
<br><br>

"...Woof," <<he>> tries again.
<br><br>

The Black Wolf lays its head back down.
<br><br>

Bailey turns to you. <span class="gold">"One week,"</span> <<he>> says. Then <<he>> backs slowly out of the cave, never breaking eye contact with the pack.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Wolf Cave]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Bailey Cat Ears
<<effects>>
<<person1>>

<<if $renttime lte 0>>
	You bring it up. Bailey looks at you.
	<br><br>
	"You owe me money," <<he>> says. "Pay your rent first. Then we can discuss your hobbies."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Leave|Orphanage]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<set _price to 200000>>

	<<if not setup.inflation.canAfford(_price, "catEars")>>
		"I'll pay you to put on cat ears," you say.
		<br><br>
		<<if $bailey_catears is undefined or $bailey_catears is 0>>
			"Cat ears." <<He>> repeats. "<span class="gold"><<printprice _price>></span>."
			<br><br>
			You don't have <span class="gold"><<printprice _price>></span>.
		<<else>>
			"Cat ears." <<He>> repeats. "<span class="gold"><<printprice _price>></span>."
			<br><br>
			You don't have <span class="gold"><<printprice _price>></span>.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Leave|Orphanage]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<if $bailey_catears is undefined or $bailey_catears is 0>>
			<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
				"W-Will you put on cat ears if I give you <span class="gold"><<printprice _price>></span>?" you ask. "P-please?"
			<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
				"I have <span class="gold"><<printprice _price>></span> for you if you put on cat ears." You shake the money in your hands towards Bailey. "Come on, it's easy money."
			<<else>>
				"If I give you <span class="gold"><<printprice _price>></span>, will you put on cat ears for me to see?" you ask. "I won't tell anyone."
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			Bailey looks at the money. Then at you. <<His>> expression doesn't change.
			<br><br>
			<<if $bailey_dom gte 70>>
				"Everything has a price," <<he>> says with a shrug, taking the money. "Fine."
			<<elseif $bailey_dom gte 30>>
				With a look of undiluted exasperation, <<he>> snatches the money out of your hand. "Fine."
			<<else>>
				<<He>> snatches the money out of your hand with a sneer. "Damn brat."
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			<<money -200000 "catEars">>
			<br><br>
			<<link [[Next|Bailey Cat Ears Scene]]>><</link>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			<<if $bailey_catears gte 3>>
				"You're paying for my patience at this point," <<he>> says before you even open your mouth. <<He>> holds out <<his>> hand.
				<br><br>
				You set <span class="gold"><<printprice _price>></span> on the desk.
			<<elseif $bailey_catears gte 2>>
				The cat ears are already on <<his>> desk when you walk in. <<He>> doesn't look up from <<his>> paperwork.
				<br><br>
				"I anticipated this," <<he>> says.
				<br><br>
				You set <span class="gold"><<printprice _price>></span> on the desk.
			<<else>>
				Bailey sighs before you say a word. <<He>> opens the drawer.
				<br><br>
				You set <span class="gold"><<printprice _price>></span> on the desk.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			<<money -200000 "catEars">>
			<br><br>
			<<link [[Next|Bailey Cat Ears Scene]]>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>


:: Bailey Cat Ears Scene
<<effects>>
<<person1>>

<<if $bailey_catears is undefined or $bailey_catears is 0>>
	<<He>> opens <<his>> desk drawer. <<He>> fumbles past its contents until <<he>> finds something buried deep. <<He>> produces a pair of cat ears. Black. Slightly dusty. <<He>> had likely confiscated them from an orphan in the past.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> puts them on. <<He>> doesn't adjust them. They remain crooked on <<his>> head while <<he>> crosses <<his>> arms and glares at you.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> checks <<his>> watch.
	<br><br>
	You take in every detail. The cat ears on Bailey's head. <<His>> flat expression. <<His>> complete refusal to acknowledge the absurdity of the situation.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> removes them and tosses them back in the drawer.
	<br><br>
	"This never happened," <<he>> says. "Get out."<<stress -6>><<lstress>><<trauma -2>><<ltrauma>>
<<else>>
	<<He>> puts on the ears. Arms crossed. Same expression as last time. Same expression as always.
	<br><br>
	<<if $bailey_catears gte 3>>
		<<He>> checks <<his>> watch twice.
		<br><br>
		"Your thirty seconds started when you walked in," <<he>> says.
	<<elseif $bailey_catears gte 2>>
		<<He>> stands there. You can hear the clock ticking.
		<br><br>
		"I've started charging by the second," <<he>> says. <<He>> hasn't.
	<<else>>
		<<He>> stands there. <<He>> waits.
		<br><br>
		"You're wasting daylight," <<he>> says.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<He>> removes the ears. <<He>> doesn't fold them this time. <<He>> drops them in the drawer and shuts it.
	<br><br>
	"Out," <<he>> says.<<stress -6>><<lstress>><<trauma -2>><<ltrauma>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $bailey_catears is undefined>>
	<<set $bailey_catears to 1>>
<<else>>
	<<set $bailey_catears += 1>>
<</if>>

<<link [[Leave|Orphanage]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
